      "writtenOn": "2023-05-17T00:25:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Again, looks very invasive into the default kernel\u0027s memory management. Please post reasons and performance benefits in the bug.\n\nThe patch should be split into smaller logical pieces each with its own description and reasoning.\nFor page pooling:\nandroid_rvh_alloc_pages\nandroid_rvh_free_pages\nandroid_rvh_si_mem_available\n\nFor pcp bypass:\nandroid_rvh_buddy_rmqueue\n\nFor ALLOC_HARDER:\nandroid_rvh_gfp_to_alloc_flags\n\nFor fault_around:\nandroid_rvh_do_fault_around",
      "revId": "9ae9ab017d9d7805bf3e5b994dc8d4825cb569ff",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
